    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued October 18 at 12:31PM PDT until October 20 at 9:00AM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Dangerous rip currents and breaking waves due to elevated\nsurf of 3 to 6 feet expected.\n\n* WHERE...Ventura County Beaches, Malibu Coast and Los Angeles\nCounty Beaches.\n\n* WHEN...Through Tuesday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...There is an increased risk of ocean drowning. Rip\ncurrents can pull swimmers and surfers out to sea. Waves can\nwash people off beaches and rocks, and capsize small boats\nnearshore.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Minor beach erosion and tidal overflows\nmay occur across south-facing beaches especially in the Long\nBeach area.",
    "instruction": "Remain out of the water due to hazardous swimming conditions, or\nstay near occupied lifeguard towers. Rock jetties can be deadly\nin such conditions, stay off the rocks.",
    "response": "Avoid",
